    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Three parallel vectors: <computeroutput><ref refid="class_basic_poly_ad5e6df290f9c75deda9574600ef77ad5_1ad5e6df290f9c75deda9574600ef77ad5" kindref="member">mCoefficients</ref></computeroutput> (<computeroutput>mpz_class</computeroutput> per term), <computeroutput><ref refid="class_basic_poly_acbd02ae9564e3b122435ce126fc64b02_1acbd02ae9564e3b122435ce126fc64b02" kindref="member">mComponents</ref></computeroutput> (free-module component per term, all-zero when empty), and <computeroutput><ref refid="class_basic_poly_a62c9a46760d40a4eb2bfc0bdf2b5d75c_1a62c9a46760d40a4eb2bfc0bdf2b5d75c" kindref="member">mMonomials</ref></computeroutput> (a concatenation of varpower monomials, each prefixed by its length). Used by the stream-based polynomial I/O paths (<computeroutput><ref refid="_basic_poly_list_8hpp_a24fbc5f5eec7472cd3ee08f9f323741e_1a24fbc5f5eec7472cd3ee08f9f323741e" kindref="member">BasicPolyList</ref></computeroutput>) and as a portable interchange format when polynomials need to live outside the engine&apos;s typed <computeroutput><ref refid="class_ring" kindref="compound">Ring</ref></computeroutput> machinery. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
